From: ADP Monitor Windows engine build <276656355+alexfused@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: Take root certificates only from the Keychain on macOS.

On macOS, crypt32 reads the root certificates from the Keychain's trust
settings, and only if that gives none it scans certificate files and
folders meant for Linux and BSD, among them /usr/local/share/certs/. On
an Intel Mac /usr/local is Homebrew's folder, writable without
administrator rights, so leave the fallback list out on macOS.

This change is licensed like Wine: LGPL-2.1-or-later.
---

--- a/dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c
@@ -944,6 +944,9 @@
     }
 }
 
+/* Not on macOS: there the Keychain's trust settings are the only source of root certificates
+ * (on an Intel Mac /usr/local is Homebrew's folder, writable without administrator rights). */
+#ifndef __APPLE__
 static const char * const CRYPT_knownLocations[] = {
  "/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt",
  "/etc/ssl/certs",
@@ -953,6 +956,7 @@
  "/etc/sfw/openssl/certs",
  "/etc/security/cacerts",  /* Android */
 };
+#endif
 
 static void load_root_certs(void)
 {
@@ -989,10 +993,10 @@
             CFRelease(certs);
         }
     }
-#endif
-
+#else
     for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(CRYPT_knownLocations) && list_empty(&root_cert_list); i++)
         import_certs_from_path( CRYPT_knownLocations[i], TRUE );
+#endif
 }
 
 static NTSTATUS enum_root_certs( void *args )
